      "content": "Music, B.A.",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "aaed8047-00d1-4223-9190-01981eb30093",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 1,
      "content": "ABOUT THE MAJOR The music major prepares students for professional careers and/or graduate study in the discipline of music. The major combines music theory and history with practical participation in a variety of musical activities, including performance ensembles and private music study. Students graduating with the music major can find employment in public school teaching, private studio instruction, performance, church ministries, the recording industry and many other music business enterprises. Some professions require additional music training and student are encouraged to continue studies at the graduate level or in specialized schools. **Agreement does not include all required courses for the major at FPU** This agreement lists courses that are prerequisites or may be completed prior to transfer to satisfy major requirements. All transfer courses must be completed with a grade of C- or better, and students must complete a minimum of 18 units in the major at FPU. Please contact an academic advisor to discuss the recommended sequence of courses, including courses that may count for both GE and major requirements. To view the full degree requirements, please refer to the Undergraduate Catalog: https://catalog.fresno.edu/index.php .",
      "contentHtml": "<p><strong style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(22, 43, 132);\">ABOUT THE MAJOR</strong></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The music major prepares students for professional careers and/or graduate study in the discipline of music. The major combines music theory and history with practical participation in a variety of musical activities, including performance ensembles and private music study. Students graduating with the music major can find employment in public school teaching, private studio instruction, performance, church ministries, the recording industry and many other music business enterprises. Some professions require additional music training and student are encouraged to continue studies at the graduate level or in specialized schools.</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(169, 62, 58);\">﻿**Agreement does not include all required courses for the major at FPU**</strong></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">This agreement lists courses that are prerequisites or may be completed prior to transfer to satisfy major requirements. All transfer courses must be completed with a grade of C- or better, and students must complete a minimum of 18 units in the major at FPU. Please contact an academic advisor to discuss the recommended sequence of courses, including courses that may count for both GE and major requirements.&nbsp;To view the full degree requirements, please refer to the Undergraduate Catalog: </span><a href=\"https://catalog.fresno.edu/index.php\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px;\">https://catalog.fresno.edu/index.php</a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">.</span></p>"
    }
